WEBVTT

00:07.616 --> 00:09.376
[If you don't turn yourself in,
your limbs will rot and you'll die]

00:37.833 --> 00:41.233
[All characters and events are fictional,
and any resemblance is coincidental]

00:41.233 --> 00:43.867
[Scenes with children and animals were filmed
safely under professional supervision]

00:43.867 --> 00:47.700
[Law and Order, Positive Change]
You're back. What about your paper?

00:47.700 --> 00:49.400
[With a dream, you can start again]
Thanks to you, it went well.

00:50.100 --> 00:52.733
Did you solve the riddle I gave you?

00:58.233 --> 01:00.333
[Murder: 12+2, Rape: 19, Attempted: 15]
12 plus 2.

01:00.333 --> 01:02.900
That makes 14 murders in total.

01:02.900 --> 01:05.900
Are you saying there are
five more unknown murders?

01:05.900 --> 01:09.567
I knew you'd figure it out, Professor.

01:11.200 --> 01:15.233
I'll admit to all acts related to
the nine cases already known.

01:15.233 --> 01:18.633
And I'll honestly confess the rest as well.

01:18.633 --> 01:20.500
But

01:20.500 --> 01:23.567
only if you tell me something, Professor.

01:23.567 --> 01:24.667
Tell you about what?

01:24.667 --> 01:26.367
About you, Professor.

01:26.367 --> 01:27.733
You said you lost everything.

01:27.733 --> 01:31.267
Tell me exactly what you lost.

01:31.267 --> 01:32.900
For each answer,

01:34.933 --> 01:37.667
one hidden murder.

01:37.667 --> 01:39.367
Fair enough, isn't it?

01:41.533 --> 01:44.800
[Murder: 12+2, Rape: 19, Attempted: 15]

01:55.100 --> 01:57.430
If you're not willing to talk,

01:57.430 --> 02:00.200
I'll take my secret to the grave.

02:03.000 --> 02:05.967
Alright, let's do that.

02:07.633 --> 02:10.267
Now, it's getting interesting.

02:11.500 --> 02:13.433
Start with your side of the story.

02:13.433 --> 02:16.100
What exactly did you lose?

02:19.767 --> 02:23.167
I lost my friend.

02:30.467 --> 02:32.567
You've done a great job.

02:32.567 --> 02:35.067
I knew you'd pull it off, Prosecutor Cha.

02:35.833 --> 02:37.933
[Episode 6]
It's all thanks to you, sir.

02:37.933 --> 02:42.200
Now that we've identified the suspect,
catching him will be easy.

02:42.200 --> 02:44.833
Now I can finally get some peace of mind.

03:01.000 --> 03:03.067
What are you staring at so intently?

03:08.867 --> 03:11.567
Do you see this date?

03:11.567 --> 03:14.100
[December 13, 1987]
That's the day Choi In Sook went missing.

03:14.100 --> 03:17.067
- What?
- When Choi In Sook was murdered,

03:17.733 --> 03:19.967
Ki Beom was with me.

03:19.967 --> 03:22.767
Then why is Park Ae Sook's purse
in the bookstore?

03:23.767 --> 03:25.567
If it was not Lee Ki Beom...

03:28.500 --> 03:29.824
Could it be

03:29.824 --> 03:31.567
Lee Ki Beom's brother?

03:36.900 --> 03:38.933
Hey, what do you mean?

03:38.933 --> 03:41.767
Are you saying
he might not be the real killer?

03:42.533 --> 03:44.813
When Choi In Sook was murdered,

03:44.813 --> 03:46.080
Ki Beom was with me.

03:46.080 --> 03:47.700
[Wedding Reception
December 13, 1987]

03:47.700 --> 03:49.833
Just give me more time.

03:49.833 --> 03:52.000
Look, I've got a press conference
in 10 minutes.

03:52.000 --> 03:54.033
I was about to announce
we've identified the suspect.

03:54.033 --> 03:57.600
Why rush a press conference
like this all of a sudden?

03:57.600 --> 04:01.100
You're the one who wanted to rush this case.

04:01.100 --> 04:02.567
When did I say that?

04:02.567 --> 04:04.433
Anyway, cover this up.

04:04.433 --> 04:05.500
If not... oh, right.

04:05.500 --> 04:06.900
Hasn't your stab wound split open yet?

04:06.900 --> 04:08.333
Should I open it up again for you?

04:08.333 --> 04:10.567
Hey, hey!

04:10.567 --> 04:13.900
Wow, you're really
repaying kindness like this?

04:13.900 --> 04:16.833
Anyway, cover it up!
Just be vague about it, okay?

04:16.833 --> 04:18.133
You're good at that. I'm off!

04:18.133 --> 04:19.567
Cover what up?

04:19.567 --> 04:20.600
Just cover that up!

04:20.600 --> 04:22.200
Hey, Tae Joo!

04:46.567 --> 04:49.067
So what are you going to announce today?

04:49.067 --> 04:51.500
Have you found the serial killer?

04:59.600 --> 05:01.567
We have identified

05:01.567 --> 05:05.867
a prime suspect in the seven murder cases
that have occurred in Kangseng

05:05.867 --> 05:09.100
over the past two years, but...

05:09.100 --> 05:10.867
- "But"?
- "But"?

05:10.867 --> 05:13.867
Is he a prime suspect or not?

05:18.833 --> 05:20.600
Father!

05:28.900 --> 05:31.433
[Bang Kyung Moon Clinic]

05:31.433 --> 05:33.100
Drop by sometime.

05:33.100 --> 05:35.000
This old man gets lonely.

05:35.000 --> 05:37.400
I know you're even busier than I am.

05:38.600 --> 05:40.633
There must be a patient named Lee Ki Hwan.

05:40.633 --> 05:41.933
Let me see the list.

05:41.933 --> 05:45.233
- Just a moment.
- Isn't that Detective Kang?

05:45.233 --> 05:46.900
- Detective?
- Yeah.

05:46.900 --> 05:49.733
The detective in charge of
the serial murders.

05:52.667 --> 05:55.200
Please introduce me to him.

05:55.200 --> 05:56.767
Huh?

05:56.767 --> 05:58.267
[Dr. Jo Yun Seok
from Korea Atomic Energy Research Institute]

05:58.267 --> 06:00.267
I'm Jo Yun Seok.

06:00.900 --> 06:02.533
Please have a seat.

06:04.633 --> 06:07.967
Why is someone from the nuclear
research institute looking for me?

06:07.967 --> 06:11.867
I was hoping to explain some
scientific methods that could help

06:11.867 --> 06:13.600
narrow down the suspects.

06:13.600 --> 06:15.456
Is there such a method?

06:16.800 --> 06:20.700
It's a method called 'radioisotope analysis.'

06:20.700 --> 06:22.233
What can you do with that?

06:22.233 --> 06:24.700
Just like our fingerprints are all different,

06:24.700 --> 06:29.100
the elemental composition of human hair
also varies from person to person.

06:29.100 --> 06:30.900
So you're saying

06:30.900 --> 06:34.100
you can irradiate the suspect's
and the killer's hair,

06:34.100 --> 06:39.267
and based on the elements released,
determine if they're the same person?

06:39.267 --> 06:44.867
Yes, based on the results, we might infer
their occupation or living environment.

06:46.733 --> 06:49.367
Have you ever identified
a suspect using this method?

06:49.367 --> 06:50.667
No.

06:50.667 --> 06:53.400
Has it ever been accepted
as evidence in court?

06:54.133 --> 06:56.667
Well, not yet.

06:57.933 --> 07:01.200
Everything has a first time, doesn't it?

07:01.200 --> 07:02.528
- A first time...
- Today,

07:02.528 --> 07:05.033
the Kangseng Branch
of the Muwon District Prosecutors' Office

07:05.033 --> 07:09.533
announced they have identified
a serial killer behind seven murders of women

07:09.533 --> 07:11.767
over the past two years.

07:11.767 --> 07:17.100
The suspect is a man in his 20s,
surnamed Lee, who lives in Kangseng

07:17.100 --> 07:19.667
and runs a bookstore.

07:19.667 --> 07:23.633
The murder of a middle school girl
on the 22nd

07:23.633 --> 07:26.733
has also been confirmed as his doing.

07:26.733 --> 07:28.333
Looks like you don't need my proposal.

07:28.333 --> 07:29.367
The crime scene is

07:29.367 --> 07:32.000
- That darn lunatic.
- around Jangseong village.

07:32.000 --> 07:37.167
He targeted women who were
usually alone on their way home,

07:37.167 --> 07:40.133
abducted them,
restrained their hands and feet

07:40.133 --> 07:43.100
to prevent resistance,
sexually assaulted them,

07:43.100 --> 07:47.133
and then brutally murdered them.

07:47.833 --> 07:49.383
As the suspect

07:49.383 --> 07:51.267
continues to kill,

07:51.267 --> 07:53.867
the interval between crimes has decreased,

07:53.867 --> 07:56.167
and bodies were also
found around the village...

07:56.167 --> 07:57.600
Mother, please stay strong...

07:57.600 --> 08:00.167
Take it away!

08:00.167 --> 08:02.767
What should I do?

08:04.000 --> 08:08.567
We have clearly classified this case
as a serial murder case,

08:08.567 --> 08:11.700
and will conduct a thorough investigation
to determine the full facts,

08:11.700 --> 08:14.233
ensure such incidents do not happen again,

08:14.233 --> 08:19.700
and remain fully committed
to justice and accountability.

08:19.700 --> 08:22.867
The prosecution has placed the suspect,
Mr. Lee, on a public wanted list

08:22.867 --> 08:26.700
and stated they will do their utmost
to apprehend him quickly.

08:26.700 --> 08:29.833
Thus, attention is now focused on
whether this will bring an end

08:29.833 --> 08:33.067
to the serial murder case
that has left Kangseng in fear

08:33.067 --> 08:35.633
over the past two years.

08:35.633 --> 08:39.200
This has been Reporter Kim Ji Hun from KBS.

08:45.000 --> 08:46.933
It's ginger tea.

08:56.067 --> 08:59.200
The aroma is nice.

09:00.333 --> 09:03.433
What brings you here?
You must be busy with election preparation.

09:03.433 --> 09:08.033
Let's finalize your marriage arrangement
with Chairman Kim soon.

09:09.167 --> 09:11.600
That can wait until after the election.

09:11.600 --> 09:14.100
How do you know
how the election will turn out?

09:14.100 --> 09:17.333
We need to set a date in advance,
so there's no backing out.

09:23.367 --> 09:27.067
So you found the serial killer?

09:27.067 --> 09:28.667
Yes.

09:29.367 --> 09:30.967
You've worked hard.

09:36.833 --> 09:38.500
Father.

09:41.067 --> 09:43.600
Cha Si Young, you...

09:46.100 --> 09:47.667
Detective Kang!

09:47.667 --> 09:50.500
How rude of you! I have a guest here.

09:50.500 --> 09:53.533
I don't have time
to take a number and wait, sir.

09:53.533 --> 09:55.033
Could I borrow Prosecutor Cha?

09:55.033 --> 09:57.700
Alright, I understand.
Let's talk later, okay?

09:57.700 --> 10:00.160
If official business is urgent,

10:00.160 --> 10:01.933
this old man should step aside.

10:01.933 --> 10:05.000
No, Father, you don't have to do that.

10:05.000 --> 10:06.833
- Just a moment...
- You don't need to come out.

10:09.867 --> 10:11.467
Wait.

10:15.633 --> 10:18.200
Have we met somewhere before?

10:27.833 --> 10:30.433
I don't think so.

10:31.800 --> 10:34.000
I must be mistaken.

10:36.067 --> 10:37.867
I'll call you.

10:37.867 --> 10:39.467
Wait, Father...

10:44.986 --> 10:46.767
[An Upright Republic of Korea]

10:46.767 --> 10:48.567
Hey!

10:48.567 --> 10:50.733
What's up with the press conference?

10:50.733 --> 10:53.567
I told you we need to investigate further.

10:53.567 --> 10:57.133
I thought about it too.

10:57.133 --> 10:59.133
The date on that photo of Lee Ki Beom.

10:59.133 --> 11:03.267
It's the date of Choi In Sook's
disappearance, not her death.

11:03.267 --> 11:07.300
The body was too decomposed
to determine the exact time of death.

11:07.300 --> 11:08.967
- What are you saying...
- And also,

11:08.967 --> 11:13.000
like her mother said,
Choi In Sook might have run away.

11:13.000 --> 11:15.000
There are many possibilities.

11:15.767 --> 11:17.567
What's your excuse for this right now?

11:17.567 --> 11:19.467
Why are you being
so unreasonable all of a sudden?

11:19.467 --> 11:21.633
Who's being unreasonable right now?

11:21.633 --> 11:23.567
Is it because of Sun Young?

11:25.833 --> 11:27.800
What do you mean by that?

11:28.433 --> 11:30.933
Sun Young is pregnant
with Lee Ki Beom's child, right?

11:32.767 --> 11:35.633
Jeez... I knew it.

11:35.633 --> 11:39.833
Back at Lee Ki Beom's place,
I wondered if it might be morning sickness.

11:41.408 --> 11:44.433
What is Sun Young going to do now?

11:44.433 --> 11:46.900
Why are you even bringing her up now?

11:46.900 --> 11:48.133
Hey.

11:48.133 --> 11:52.200
You want to save him because he's the father
of your future niece or nephew, don't you?

11:52.200 --> 11:53.767
What are you even talking about?

11:53.767 --> 11:57.333
If not him, then is there
another suspect besides Lee Ki Beom?

11:57.333 --> 11:58.967
That's...

12:00.633 --> 12:04.033
It's certain the suspect is
someone around Lee Ki Beom.

12:04.033 --> 12:05.633
So I'll widen the investigation...

12:05.633 --> 12:08.400
Bring me the real killer!

12:08.400 --> 12:11.400
Bring me evidence and convince me, you punk!

12:12.333 --> 12:15.100
That's the order of things, Tae Joo!

12:21.767 --> 12:23.867
You darn commie punk!

12:23.867 --> 12:27.200
[Capital 1-2]
Spill it quick, you punk!

12:27.200 --> 12:30.167
Let's end this today.

12:33.200 --> 12:37.733
I've treated you nicely all this time.

12:37.733 --> 12:39.467
Let's start again.

12:42.167 --> 12:46.400
Darn it, it's driving me crazy.

12:47.200 --> 12:50.800
I told you to bring him in, not beat him up!

12:50.800 --> 12:52.800
I'm sorry, Prosecutor Cha.

12:53.700 --> 12:55.067
Take that out of his mouth.

12:55.067 --> 12:56.700
Yes, sir!

13:06.867 --> 13:09.167
So, your bookstore has a lot of things?

13:10.000 --> 13:11.167
You heard, right?

13:11.167 --> 13:13.667
What was found in your bookstore?

13:13.667 --> 13:15.767
Communist books were found,

13:15.767 --> 13:18.100
and a victim's purse too.

13:18.800 --> 13:21.067
It's like a treasure trove, huh?

13:23.933 --> 13:26.200
I didn't do anything.

13:28.000 --> 13:29.700
What did you say?

13:30.667 --> 13:32.433
Say that again.

13:33.200 --> 13:35.133
It wasn't me.

13:38.567 --> 13:40.633
He might be telling the truth.

13:41.800 --> 13:42.867
Maybe it's not him!

13:42.867 --> 13:44.867
No,

13:44.867 --> 13:45.900
that can't be.

13:45.900 --> 13:47.833
Look at his eyes!

13:47.833 --> 13:50.800
Do they look like the eyes of a liar?

13:50.800 --> 13:55.733
Jeez, this guy isn't the serial killer.

13:55.733 --> 13:58.267
He's just a commie!

13:59.933 --> 14:02.767
Then who is the suspect, Mr. Cha?

14:02.767 --> 14:05.664
It must be his brother! The bookstore
belongs to his brother, right?

14:08.133 --> 14:09.233
That makes sense.

14:09.233 --> 14:14.167
Good grief, how did your mother
raise her children like this?

14:14.167 --> 14:17.933
One's a serial killer,
and the other's a commie.

14:17.933 --> 14:20.367
In that case, your mother's
the root of it all, you know.

14:20.367 --> 14:22.100
Giving birth to monsters like you...

14:22.100 --> 14:25.267
Shut up! Stop talking nonsense!

14:25.900 --> 14:30.367
Calm down and keep this in mind.

14:30.367 --> 14:34.567
This is how the world
will see your mother from now on.

14:38.367 --> 14:40.867
What are you waiting for?
Why aren't you bringing in his brother?

14:40.867 --> 14:42.967
- Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

14:42.967 --> 14:45.900
No, not my brother!

14:45.900 --> 14:48.167
My brother isn't that kind of person!

14:48.167 --> 14:49.867
Then who is it?

15:03.767 --> 15:05.500
Tell me who it is.

15:07.200 --> 15:08.833
Promise me,

15:10.500 --> 15:12.367
if I confess,

15:13.533 --> 15:15.967
you won't touch my family.

15:18.967 --> 15:22.000
This punk is threatening a prosecutor, huh?

15:22.000 --> 15:23.100
Promise me!

15:23.100 --> 15:24.900
You punk.

15:28.067 --> 15:32.233
In return, there's something
you have to promise me too.

15:34.933 --> 15:37.967
[Korea Atomic Energy Research Institute]

15:39.567 --> 15:41.300
Oh, hello.

15:41.300 --> 15:43.000
Welcome.

15:44.533 --> 15:46.304
Sorry,

15:46.304 --> 15:50.267
but to be honest, I didn't come here
because I trust your test.

15:50.933 --> 15:52.960
I came here

15:52.960 --> 15:54.400
simply because I'm at a loss,

15:54.400 --> 15:57.767
hoping I might get lucky and find something.

15:57.767 --> 16:01.667
Yes, I understand what you mean.

16:02.633 --> 16:04.733
This is the suspect's hair.

16:04.733 --> 16:06.467
Please analyze it.

16:15.300 --> 16:16.967
If you look here,

16:16.967 --> 16:19.520
[Radioactive Isotope Analysis Report]
compared to average, titanium, sodium,

16:19.520 --> 16:21.467
and chlorine are significantly higher.

16:21.467 --> 16:24.400
Is there a special reason for that?

16:24.400 --> 16:26.200
High titanium levels would mean

16:26.200 --> 16:29.667
the person has been exposed
to a titanium-rich environment.

16:29.667 --> 16:34.200
He could be a worker in a factory
that handles alloys or welding.

16:35.733 --> 16:37.967
What about sodium and chlorine?

16:37.967 --> 16:41.200
Those are the main components of sweat.

16:41.200 --> 16:43.733
He's likely someone who sweats a lot.

16:44.733 --> 16:48.000
So you're saying the killer could be

16:48.000 --> 16:49.824
a factory worker

16:49.824 --> 16:53.600
who's constantly
drenched in sweat, is that it?

16:53.600 --> 16:55.200
Probably.

16:57.800 --> 17:01.633
[Occupation: factory worker]

17:03.433 --> 17:05.967
Go stay at your parents' for a while.

17:05.967 --> 17:10.900
But will you and your mother be okay?

17:10.900 --> 17:12.333
You know how stubborn my mother is.

17:12.333 --> 17:15.100
She's not the type to
leave Ki Beom alone and go somewhere.

17:18.767 --> 17:20.100
Please take care of her.

17:20.100 --> 17:22.100
Don't worry about us, Ki Hwan.

17:47.233 --> 17:53.533
[Murderer, get out]

18:07.610 --> 18:11.130
[Korean Novel]

18:17.067 --> 18:24.067
[Kangseng Bookstore]

18:30.633 --> 18:32.233
Tae Joo!

18:33.967 --> 18:38.000
Where have you been?
Hurry up and clean this up.

18:38.000 --> 18:39.700
Oh, okay.

18:48.700 --> 18:53.800
I don't know how they found out,
but both the house and bookstore are a mess.

18:57.500 --> 18:59.800
How is your mother doing?

18:59.800 --> 19:01.767
She's been laid up in bed
from the shock, of course.

19:01.767 --> 19:05.633
I told her to stay at a relative's,
but she won't listen.

19:10.300 --> 19:12.900
Lee Ki Hwan isn't type B.

19:12.900 --> 19:14.900
He is type AB.

19:17.367 --> 19:20.933
[Lee Ki Hwan, Type AB]

19:32.367 --> 19:35.233
Ki Hwan, actually...

19:36.200 --> 19:38.400
What is it?

19:38.400 --> 19:40.733
Oh my, you should be careful.

19:40.733 --> 19:42.333
It's just a small cut.

19:42.333 --> 19:43.633
It's not small at all. Jeez.

19:43.633 --> 19:45.400
Hold still. It's bleeding a lot.

19:45.400 --> 19:47.067
- No, I'm fine.
- Press on it.

19:55.467 --> 19:57.100
What are you doing?

20:01.167 --> 20:03.367
What's with that blood?

20:05.767 --> 20:07.600
What is this?

20:11.100 --> 20:12.567
Ji Won, hey!

20:12.567 --> 20:14.500
Ji Won, I'll explain everything.

20:14.500 --> 20:15.933
What were you going to do
with Ki Hwan's blood?

20:15.933 --> 20:17.967
Are you trying to check
his blood type or something?

20:17.967 --> 20:20.833
- This is a misunderstanding.
- Misunderstanding?

20:20.833 --> 20:24.433
Ki Beom wasn't enough, and now it's Ki Hwan?

20:24.433 --> 20:27.133
What's the evidence this time? What is it?

20:27.133 --> 20:29.633
Did you find evidence in the bookstore?

20:32.333 --> 20:33.933
The purse?

20:38.467 --> 20:40.133
Is that it?

20:41.133 --> 20:44.300
You're suspecting me because of that?

20:44.300 --> 20:47.333
Purse? What purse?

20:49.767 --> 20:52.133
Tae Joo, is that true?

20:55.467 --> 20:57.120
So you

20:57.120 --> 21:00.033
really came for that,
to find out my blood type?

21:00.800 --> 21:04.200
You could have just asked. I can tell you.

21:04.200 --> 21:05.800
I'm type AB.

21:06.600 --> 21:09.767
If you don't believe me,
take this and get it tested.

21:10.433 --> 21:12.133
Enough, man.

21:14.667 --> 21:16.500
Yeah, honestly,

21:17.700 --> 21:19.567
I suspected you.

21:20.500 --> 21:22.633
But not anymore, though.

21:27.500 --> 21:30.567
I'm sorry, I'm really...

21:34.567 --> 21:36.367
- Are you okay?
- Are you okay?

21:37.033 --> 21:38.200
Are you alright?

21:38.200 --> 21:39.367
- Let me see.
- Let me see.

21:39.367 --> 21:41.033
- Let me see.
- Jeez.

21:41.033 --> 21:42.833
Let me see, hurry.

21:45.100 --> 21:48.067
How did the victim's belonging get here?

21:48.067 --> 21:51.200
Unless someone deliberately placed it here.

21:51.200 --> 21:55.067
I don't know where things went wrong, either.

21:57.400 --> 21:59.933
We need to catch the real killer,
so Ki Beom can clear his name.

21:59.933 --> 22:01.533
That's the situation now.

22:02.933 --> 22:05.633
That punk is definitely close to Ki Beom.

22:06.400 --> 22:10.267
Has Ki Beom been hanging out
with shady people?

22:10.267 --> 22:11.300
Like someone with a criminal record...

22:11.300 --> 22:15.400
No. They are all people
he's known since childhood.

22:17.533 --> 22:22.533
He could be a worker in a factory
that handles alloys or welding.

22:22.533 --> 22:24.567
Any friend working at a factory?

22:24.567 --> 22:25.867
Yeah, there is one.

22:25.867 --> 22:27.500
Why the factory?

22:29.400 --> 22:30.733
Where is it?

22:30.733 --> 22:32.567
Ilwon Industries.

22:37.900 --> 22:40.800
[Testing Facility]
Excuse me, is there a guy named Jung Soo?

22:40.800 --> 22:42.433
Over there.

23:19.000 --> 23:21.700
[Ilwon Industries]

23:21.700 --> 23:23.233
Here it is.

23:23.233 --> 23:25.133
Yes, thank you.

23:25.933 --> 23:30.700
[Lee Jung Soo, Type O]

23:31.567 --> 23:33.300
Type O...

23:34.176 --> 23:35.333
They're here!

23:35.333 --> 23:36.633
What was your motive?

23:36.633 --> 23:39.400
Is it true you chased down and murdered
a schoolgirl who visited the bookstore?

23:39.400 --> 23:40.933
Please move aside.

23:40.933 --> 23:44.367
Are you the real killer
in the serial murder case?

23:46.367 --> 23:48.367
Answer me!

23:49.733 --> 23:51.800
Just say one thing.

23:52.600 --> 23:54.700
He is not saying anything.

23:55.866 --> 23:57.473
Did you get anything?

23:57.473 --> 23:59.330
- No, no...
- Jeez.

24:00.367 --> 24:03.633
How does it feel? Relieving, isn't it?

24:03.633 --> 24:05.833
That's what confession is like.

24:08.500 --> 24:10.467
Detective Kang, good timing.

24:10.467 --> 24:12.833
Lee Ki Beom just confessed to everything.

24:12.833 --> 24:14.464
[Security Interview Room]
What?

24:14.464 --> 24:15.633
Already?

24:15.633 --> 24:18.933
This little rat finally realized
he couldn't escape

24:18.933 --> 24:21.533
and spilled everything right away.

24:21.533 --> 24:22.667
I need to talk to him for a moment.

24:22.667 --> 24:23.867
No way, man.

24:23.867 --> 24:25.100
Just a minute is enough.

24:25.100 --> 24:26.700
Detective Do,

24:26.700 --> 24:28.733
let's step outside for a smoke.

24:28.733 --> 24:31.767
Okay, let's go.

24:33.333 --> 24:35.933
Oh, wait a second.

24:46.633 --> 24:48.233
Ki Beom.

24:50.233 --> 24:52.100
What happened?

24:54.067 --> 24:56.000
It's exactly as you heard.

25:00.533 --> 25:02.700
Was it really you?

25:08.533 --> 25:10.133
Answer me!

25:10.133 --> 25:12.100
Was it really you?

25:14.267 --> 25:15.900
Yes.

25:18.650 --> 25:19.776
What?

25:20.467 --> 25:22.400
Why would someone who's been
hiding so desperately

25:22.400 --> 25:25.267
suddenly confess so easily?

25:25.267 --> 25:28.200
In return, there's something
you have to promise me too.

25:28.200 --> 25:33.533
Don't bring up being detained
or anything like that.

25:34.400 --> 25:36.800
I heard evidence was found
at the bookstore, right?

25:36.800 --> 25:40.767
If I kept denying it, my brother
would inevitably be suspected.

25:41.800 --> 25:43.488
How could I

25:43.488 --> 25:45.300
do that to my family?

25:46.433 --> 25:51.967
You care so much about your family,
but you killed victims so brutally?

25:51.967 --> 25:55.167
They all had precious families too.

25:55.167 --> 25:57.533
But they aren't my family.

26:00.267 --> 26:02.133
So you...

26:02.133 --> 26:04.267
So you...

26:04.267 --> 26:08.352
So you tried to kill Sun Young too? Huh?

26:14.100 --> 26:18.240
Are you really the Ki Beom I knew?

26:37.184 --> 26:38.560
Darn it!

26:43.333 --> 26:44.967
Tae Joo.

26:45.900 --> 26:47.067
What happened?

26:47.067 --> 26:48.900
What did Ki Beom say?

26:52.933 --> 26:56.167
Ki Beom has confessed.

27:00.100 --> 27:02.200
Did you hit him?

27:02.200 --> 27:06.100
- What?
- You beat a false confession out of him!

27:07.733 --> 27:10.433
Ki Beom was brought in today.

27:10.433 --> 27:12.667
He confessed as soon as he arrived.

27:12.667 --> 27:15.133
That punk... Ki Beom is the killer!

27:15.133 --> 27:17.533
No! It's not true!

27:17.533 --> 27:19.300
He admitted it himself!

27:19.300 --> 27:20.900
He said he did it himself!

27:20.900 --> 27:24.500
You, me, all of us, we've all
been fooled by him this whole time!

27:24.500 --> 27:25.567
Get a grip!

27:25.567 --> 27:26.633
No...

27:26.633 --> 27:28.933
Don't cry. Why are you crying?

27:29.733 --> 27:31.567
No.

27:32.672 --> 27:35.533
- Sun Young.
- No...

27:37.267 --> 27:39.400
I'll find a hospital.

27:40.200 --> 27:41.900
Just get an abortion first.

27:46.400 --> 27:48.141
It's okay.

27:51.767 --> 27:53.733
- Give me a cigarette, please.
- Okay.

27:57.700 --> 28:00.767
[Kangseng Serial Killer Arrested,
Mr. Lee, 20s, Bookstore Owner]

28:00.767 --> 28:05.033
They caught the suspect even before
a special investigation team was formed?

28:05.033 --> 28:06.733
The newly assigned officers are in chaos.

28:06.733 --> 28:08.000
[Prosecutor Cha, second son of Candidate Cha]
They're asking if they should still come.

28:08.000 --> 28:10.833
What is this, all show and no substance?

28:17.667 --> 28:20.800
Hold off the assignments for those
who haven't been dispatched yet,

28:20.800 --> 28:22.933
and form the team as planned with the rest.

28:22.933 --> 28:26.167
What? What are you planning to do?

28:30.200 --> 28:31.500
It'll only take a moment.

28:31.500 --> 28:34.733
I have something important I need to say.

28:34.733 --> 28:37.933
It's no use asking me, Ms. Kang.

28:42.933 --> 28:44.800
What's going on?

28:47.033 --> 28:50.733
I... I have a favor to ask.

28:57.594 --> 28:59.900
[Security Interview Room]

28:59.900 --> 29:01.933
Sun Young.

29:01.933 --> 29:03.133
You have 5 minutes.

29:03.133 --> 29:04.233
I'll be outside.

29:04.233 --> 29:06.000
Thank you.

29:10.033 --> 29:11.700
Ki Beom.

29:15.467 --> 29:16.467
What happened?

29:16.467 --> 29:18.667
I asked the prosecutor in charge.

29:20.100 --> 29:21.700
Sun Young...

29:24.667 --> 29:26.367
Don't get involved with him.

29:26.367 --> 29:28.867
Don't even ask him for favors like this.

29:28.867 --> 29:30.833
Is that what matters right now?

29:30.833 --> 29:32.967
Why did you admit something you didn't do?

29:33.767 --> 29:36.133
That wasn't you!

29:39.267 --> 29:41.533
How can you smile at a time like this?

29:43.300 --> 29:45.733
You still believe me now?

29:45.733 --> 29:48.667
Even when I say I'm a murderer,

29:49.300 --> 29:50.933
you still trust me?

30:01.967 --> 30:03.567
Ki Beom.

30:11.067 --> 30:13.300
We're having a child.

30:16.767 --> 30:18.500
What?

30:20.767 --> 30:26.167
I don't know why you're lying, but...

30:29.600 --> 30:33.000
if you think of our unborn child,

30:34.433 --> 30:37.967
if you're not ashamed before our child,

30:39.567 --> 30:41.600
fight until the end.

30:42.800 --> 30:44.500
Fight

30:45.233 --> 30:47.067
and make sure to come back.

30:49.633 --> 30:51.900
Please stay by our side.

30:51.900 --> 30:53.500
Okay?

31:09.100 --> 31:11.233
Ki Beom.

31:11.233 --> 31:13.067
I'll wait for you.

31:19.167 --> 31:20.767
Sun Young...

31:45.767 --> 31:47.500
Aren't you writing the article?

31:47.500 --> 31:49.100
What?

31:52.800 --> 31:54.833
Excuse me for a moment.

31:56.100 --> 31:59.267
So? What did you do next?

32:00.400 --> 32:02.433
After I followed her,

32:03.400 --> 32:04.992
I threatened her

32:04.992 --> 32:06.767
with a knife.

32:06.767 --> 32:08.500
And then?

32:12.767 --> 32:14.880
I said

32:14.880 --> 32:16.667
I would kill her if she didn't come with me.

32:17.786 --> 32:19.077
Right.

32:21.500 --> 32:25.767
The voice is similar, but I'm not sure.

32:26.733 --> 32:29.600
"The voice is similar"?

32:30.233 --> 32:32.600
That's enough.

32:32.600 --> 32:34.700
Alright, you can take this back now.

32:39.000 --> 32:41.867
Even so, you've had a hard time
coming all this way.

32:41.867 --> 32:43.500
Huh?

32:44.400 --> 32:46.167
This isn't mine.

32:46.167 --> 32:48.867
It must have gotten mixed in by mistake.

32:48.867 --> 32:50.533
Please throw that away.

33:02.267 --> 33:04.833
Excuse me, Ms. Park Ae Sook?

33:06.133 --> 33:07.233
Who are you?

33:07.233 --> 33:09.200
Well...

33:09.200 --> 33:12.400
I'm Seo Ji Won, a reporter
from Kangseng Daily.

33:19.867 --> 33:23.267
Do any of these people look familiar?

33:29.067 --> 33:31.067
I don't recognize any of them.

33:31.067 --> 33:33.400
Who are they?

33:33.400 --> 33:37.900
Let's say they are people who frequented
the bookstore where your purse was found.

33:41.733 --> 33:44.400
Wasn't the suspect already caught?

33:46.600 --> 33:48.933
Doesn't it feel strange?

33:48.933 --> 33:51.167
Your ID was inside the purse.

33:51.167 --> 33:53.867
If I were the culprit,

33:53.867 --> 33:58.933
I think I'd leave that purse
in front of your house, as a warning.

33:58.933 --> 34:02.633
But why did the culprit
leave it at the bookstore?

34:06.033 --> 34:09.533
I tend to be suspicious,
so please understand.

34:15.600 --> 34:17.233
Actually,

34:18.633 --> 34:20.608
I just found this

34:20.608 --> 34:22.100
inside the purse.

34:22.100 --> 34:24.300
[Pig Café]

34:24.300 --> 34:26.500
It's not mine.

34:33.338 --> 34:34.897
[2nd Floor Information]

34:38.033 --> 34:39.767
Dad!

34:43.167 --> 34:44.967
I'm sorry!

34:46.592 --> 34:51.200
Whenever my kid sees an adult man,
he thinks it's his dad.

34:51.200 --> 34:54.100
Hae Jun, let's go.

34:56.167 --> 34:58.367
What are you waiting for? Let's go.

35:11.467 --> 35:13.567
Is Lee Ki Beom's statement almost done?

35:13.567 --> 35:15.433
Yes, would you like to see it?

35:15.433 --> 35:17.033
Why would I?

35:25.300 --> 35:27.467
Did Lee Ki Beom really give this statement?

35:27.467 --> 35:29.533
Yes, why?

35:29.533 --> 35:32.367
It's all information we already know.
And some of it doesn't even match.

35:32.367 --> 35:34.333
What do you mean it doesn't match?

35:34.333 --> 35:38.367
It says he was already wearing a handkerchief
when he abducted Kim Mi Yeon, right?

35:38.367 --> 35:40.100
It doesn't match.

35:40.867 --> 35:45.800
According to Kim Mi Yeon, the suspect
only had his hat pulled low at that time.

35:45.800 --> 35:48.833
He put on the handkerchief afterward,
before attacking Ji Won.

35:48.833 --> 35:51.067
Could he have been confused? Or maybe...

35:57.933 --> 35:59.867
What are you talking about, Ki Beom?

35:59.867 --> 36:03.500
I won't just write down
whatever you tell me anymore.

36:09.000 --> 36:11.567
You punk!

36:11.567 --> 36:14.733
You haven't been beaten lately,
so life feels easy, huh?

36:14.733 --> 36:16.467
Get up!

36:16.467 --> 36:18.933
This is why someone like you

36:18.933 --> 36:23.400
needs to be beaten every day, you punk!

36:23.400 --> 36:24.832
- What are you doing?
- Detective Kang!

36:24.832 --> 36:26.933
Move aside.

36:26.933 --> 36:28.567
Ki Beom!

36:28.567 --> 36:29.733
Darn it.

36:29.733 --> 36:31.200
Are you alright?

36:31.200 --> 36:32.992
Look at me.

36:33.667 --> 36:35.767
- Ki Beom, are you okay?
- Tae Joo.

36:35.767 --> 36:37.370
Let's go.

36:41.067 --> 36:42.700
What's wrong?

36:49.067 --> 36:50.700
What is this?

36:51.567 --> 36:53.200
This...

36:54.300 --> 36:56.733
These aren't fresh wounds
from just yesterday or today.

36:56.733 --> 36:59.300
When did you get these?

37:07.967 --> 37:12.533
You were lying about
losing Lee Ki Beom from the start, right?

37:12.533 --> 37:17.033
You were secretly imprisoning
and interrogating him all along, right?

37:18.133 --> 37:20.267
What does that matter now?
We caught the suspect.

37:20.267 --> 37:23.033
Illegal arrest!
Unlawful confinement and assault!

37:23.033 --> 37:25.733
Any confession obtained that way is invalid!

37:25.733 --> 37:28.267
If Prosecutor Cha finds out
everything you've done...

37:38.300 --> 37:40.567
So that punk ordered it, huh?

37:45.333 --> 37:48.533
What a double celebration this is.

37:48.533 --> 37:50.967
Prosecutor Cha caught a serial killer,

37:50.967 --> 37:53.600
and your approval ratings have risen.

37:55.733 --> 37:57.367
Exactly,

37:57.367 --> 37:59.567
I'm benefiting from this guy too.

37:59.567 --> 38:02.767
When I heard he had been stabbed,
my heart just sank.

38:02.767 --> 38:06.467
Anyway, you really don't hesitate
to do dangerous things.

38:06.467 --> 38:08.400
If anything like this happens again,

38:08.400 --> 38:11.633
I won't let Hee Jin marry you.

38:11.633 --> 38:12.700
Understood.

38:12.700 --> 38:14.600
Oh my, Dad.

38:14.600 --> 38:17.733
I really admire that side of Si Young.

38:17.733 --> 38:19.033
Oh my, you...

38:19.033 --> 38:20.867
Have you no shame,
right in front of Candidate Cha?

38:20.867 --> 38:24.100
No, it's fine.

38:24.100 --> 38:27.700
Hee Jin is such a sweet girl.

38:29.033 --> 38:31.600
Thank you, Father.

38:31.600 --> 38:33.200
"Father"?

38:35.200 --> 38:37.067
That sounds nice.

38:37.833 --> 38:41.067
It would've been nice
if your wife could have joined us.

38:41.067 --> 38:43.000
She's a bit unwell,

38:43.000 --> 38:45.633
but I'm sure she'll be back on her feet soon.

38:45.633 --> 38:51.667
Keeping talent like this only in Kangseng
would be a national loss, don't you think?

38:54.167 --> 38:56.800
Everyone has their purpose, I guess.

38:56.800 --> 39:01.600
Where there's a will, there's a way.

39:01.600 --> 39:06.600
Oh, how about holding the wedding
right after the election?

39:07.467 --> 39:09.633
That would be good.

39:12.000 --> 39:13.633
Please eat.

39:26.533 --> 39:30.900
Once this case is over,
prepare to move up to Seoul.

39:30.900 --> 39:32.000
Pardon?

39:32.000 --> 39:36.667
You just get ready quietly.
Chairman Kim will handle the rest.

39:36.667 --> 39:41.467
The wedding will be held in Seoul anyway,
so he'll naturally hurry it along.

39:41.467 --> 39:47.133
There's no better occasion
to greet people than family events.

39:47.133 --> 39:51.168
And Chairman Kim isn't the type
to miss such opportunities.

39:54.233 --> 39:55.833
Go home.

39:57.700 --> 40:01.333
Aren't you coming in?
Jun Young is probably waiting.

40:01.967 --> 40:03.867
I'm heading to the office.

40:12.600 --> 40:14.267
That guy.

40:27.233 --> 40:29.533
He has good eyes.

40:29.533 --> 40:33.267
He's ambitious and gutsy, but fearless.

40:35.000 --> 40:37.700
If needed, bring him to Seoul and use him.

41:03.367 --> 41:05.167
What are you doing?

41:08.467 --> 41:11.800
My little sister is sick.
Please give us a ride.

41:11.800 --> 41:13.667
- What?
- He's really...

41:13.667 --> 41:16.867
- Go home now! Hurry!
- Just to the hospital.

41:16.867 --> 41:19.033
Please give us a ride just this once.

41:21.400 --> 41:23.100
Aren't you afraid of me?

41:23.100 --> 41:26.300
I'm more afraid of something
happening to my sister.

41:32.100 --> 41:34.400
Your eyes are really...

41:38.967 --> 41:41.600
Your sister has a good older brother.

41:58.100 --> 42:00.533
Father smiled.

42:01.733 --> 42:03.500
Father...

42:04.700 --> 42:06.433
smiled.

42:19.667 --> 42:21.267
Follow me.

42:33.333 --> 42:37.600
Wow, this place is still
exactly the same as before.

42:38.667 --> 42:41.100
Are we the only ones who've changed?

42:42.133 --> 42:43.767
We...

42:48.267 --> 42:50.300
Darn you!

42:51.600 --> 42:54.667
What? Feeling nostalgic?

42:54.667 --> 42:57.633
Want to go back to the old days and fight?

42:58.600 --> 43:01.300
Hey, you punk!

43:02.133 --> 43:05.178
You punk! You deserve a beating.

43:07.488 --> 43:10.176
Darn it!

43:21.233 --> 43:23.067
What are you doing, you punk!

43:59.100 --> 44:02.433
Jeez, stop it! You lunatic!

44:14.567 --> 44:17.312
This is driving me crazy, seriously.

44:23.167 --> 44:26.767
I'd forgotten for a moment
what kind of punk you are.

44:26.767 --> 44:28.100
Honestly,

44:28.100 --> 44:29.567
no matter what kind of punk you were,

44:29.567 --> 44:32.400
I thought I could overlook everything
because you saved Sun Young.

44:32.400 --> 44:33.567
But no.

44:33.567 --> 44:37.767
You're still the same darn punk
you've always been.

44:37.767 --> 44:40.448
You're no different, you punk!

44:40.448 --> 44:42.667
That look in your eyes, huh?

44:42.667 --> 44:44.333
That darn look!

44:44.333 --> 44:46.100
You don't even know your place, you punk!

44:46.100 --> 44:48.833
You can't even tell where you belong
and where you don't.

44:48.833 --> 44:50.667
You don't even know about hierarchy!

44:50.667 --> 44:52.800
How dare you beat a prosecutor!

44:52.800 --> 44:54.933
What, is being a prosecutor
some kind of privilege?

44:54.933 --> 44:58.267
So being a prosecutor gives you
the right to detain and beat people?

44:58.267 --> 45:02.133
Oh, that is what this is about?

45:02.133 --> 45:03.333
Because of Lee Ki Beom!

45:03.333 --> 45:05.600
You're making such a big fuss over just him?

45:05.600 --> 45:09.300
- "Just him"?
- You even admitted that you were wrong!

45:09.300 --> 45:13.133
Well, no matter the means,
this time I'm right.

45:16.333 --> 45:19.000
How come you never learn?

45:19.000 --> 45:22.067
After what happened with Lee Seong Jin,
you still don't get it?

45:22.900 --> 45:25.067
Threatening people, you punk,
assaulting them,

45:25.067 --> 45:27.392
and making them nod out of fear!

45:27.392 --> 45:29.200
Darn it!

45:29.200 --> 45:31.936
Forcing confessions to avoid beating!

45:31.936 --> 45:35.567
How much truth do you think there is
in a forced confession like that?

45:40.067 --> 45:43.233
Release Lee Ki Beom.

45:43.233 --> 45:47.400
Clean up your own mess
while I'm still giving you the chance.

45:47.400 --> 45:49.567
I can't do that.

45:54.433 --> 45:56.033
Fine!

45:56.833 --> 45:58.967
Then I'll do it my way.

46:00.200 --> 46:01.833
You just wait.

46:02.567 --> 46:05.120
I have

46:05.120 --> 46:07.700
learned a lot about you.

46:16.200 --> 46:18.700
Do whatever you want, you punk!

46:27.067 --> 46:28.933
You're late, huh?

46:30.767 --> 46:32.600
You are still up.

46:33.333 --> 46:35.733
Father went straight to Seoul for work.

46:35.733 --> 46:39.667
I'll be staying here for a while.

46:43.600 --> 46:45.933
Do I need to leave?

46:46.667 --> 46:50.133
I thought you felt uncomfortable
in this house.

46:53.500 --> 46:55.200
Good night.

47:25.367 --> 47:28.567
Fine! Then I'll do it my way.

47:28.567 --> 47:30.367
You just wait.

47:30.367 --> 47:32.000
I have

47:32.867 --> 47:35.500
learned a lot about you.

47:35.500 --> 47:37.667
How ridiculous.

47:38.333 --> 47:41.133
What could you possibly do?

47:45.850 --> 47:47.706
[Kangseng Police Station]

47:50.746 --> 47:53.391
Alright.

48:00.200 --> 48:01.533
Good night.

48:01.533 --> 48:05.100
My goodness, looks like
things got pretty intense.

48:05.967 --> 48:09.533
At least you didn't embarrass the police.

48:10.167 --> 48:11.767
Pardon?

48:14.106 --> 48:16.733
Darn it!

48:16.733 --> 48:19.333
So what do you want?

48:19.333 --> 48:22.700
Lee Ki Beom is not the real killer.

48:25.067 --> 48:29.267
He was illegally confined and beaten,
leading to a false confession.

48:35.500 --> 48:38.167
- Any evidence?
- There are signs

48:38.167 --> 48:40.000
of long-term assault on Lee Ki Beom's body.

48:40.000 --> 48:42.333
Come on, not that.

48:42.333 --> 48:45.367
If he's the real killer,
illegal detention and assault aren't issues.

48:45.367 --> 48:49.000
Do you have proof he's not the real killer?

48:49.000 --> 48:52.467
He has a solid alibi
for at least one of the murder dates.

48:52.467 --> 48:53.900
Because he was with me.

48:53.900 --> 48:55.667
Could that one case be a copycat crime?

48:55.667 --> 48:57.467
No.

48:57.467 --> 48:59.008
Because there clearly is a pattern
unique to the killer

48:59.008 --> 49:01.600
that hasn't been revealed to the public.

49:01.600 --> 49:03.233
Okay.

49:06.667 --> 49:09.067
Then your task is clear.

49:09.700 --> 49:12.800
I'll prove the injustices
Lee Ki Beom has suffered

49:13.900 --> 49:16.067
and catch the real killer.

49:17.533 --> 49:20.600
What do you need from me, then?

49:20.600 --> 49:23.433
Please allow Lee Ki Beom
to receive hospital treatment.

49:27.300 --> 49:28.967
Fine.

49:32.467 --> 49:36.467
[Pig Café]

49:47.900 --> 49:49.900
You don't seem like the type to work here.

49:49.900 --> 49:52.000
Not young, either.

49:52.000 --> 49:53.100
What?

49:53.100 --> 49:56.333
Didn't you come
because you heard we were hiring girls?

49:58.533 --> 50:00.672
[Ssanghwa Tea, Honey Tea, Coffee]
I'm not here for a job, but to find someone.

50:00.672 --> 50:03.867
[Seo Ji Won, Kangseng Daily]

50:03.867 --> 50:06.867
Someone? Who?

50:09.400 --> 50:11.733
Anyone who might recognize this purse.

50:13.767 --> 50:17.133
We usually require at least
one coffee order per girl here.

50:18.333 --> 50:19.400
You want one?

50:19.400 --> 50:22.200
Yes, please give me one.

50:23.300 --> 50:24.933
I don't know.

50:30.933 --> 50:33.667
- Two?
- Not coffee.

50:33.667 --> 50:35.667
Do you have ssanghwa tea?

50:36.800 --> 50:38.967
One ssanghwa tea here!

50:42.746 --> 50:45.933
So have you ever seen this purse?

50:49.633 --> 50:52.733
This is the one that man gave me.

51:16.733 --> 51:20.000
Go to the hospital and get treatment first.

51:21.100 --> 51:22.912
Thanks,

51:22.912 --> 51:24.267
Tae Joo.

51:28.333 --> 51:30.900
The killer is someone close to you.

51:30.900 --> 51:32.933
Friend or neighbor,
he's definitely in your circle.

51:32.933 --> 51:36.233
Blood type B, with hands
as delicate as a woman's.

51:37.367 --> 51:39.433
I don't know.

51:39.433 --> 51:41.767
No one comes to mind.

51:43.300 --> 51:46.833
Can't you even remember
where you lost your handkerchief?

51:48.233 --> 51:49.967
I'm sorry.

51:51.033 --> 51:54.200
It's nothing to apologize for,
so don't bow your head.

51:56.467 --> 51:58.100
I'm sorry

51:58.767 --> 52:00.933
for letting you go through
something like that.

52:02.967 --> 52:04.864
That's not

52:04.864 --> 52:07.267
something you should
be apologizing for, either.

52:08.400 --> 52:12.667
Then do you happen to know
where the bathhouse you were held at is?

52:12.667 --> 52:14.900
No. They covered my eyes.

52:14.900 --> 52:16.767
Those darn punks.

52:18.000 --> 52:21.700
We need someone who can testify
that you were illegally detained.

52:24.733 --> 52:26.333
There is.

52:28.233 --> 52:30.033
Someone who will testify.

52:50.167 --> 52:54.567
I was making a delivery, and he
suddenly jumped out. It was a mess.

52:54.567 --> 52:57.967
You can't just suddenly jump out like that!

53:01.033 --> 53:03.700
This is too much.

53:03.700 --> 53:06.400
It's not like you did it on purpose.

53:07.400 --> 53:09.733
I'm sorry about that day.

53:09.733 --> 53:14.167
He must've felt sorry,
so he came by and left it as a gift.

53:14.167 --> 53:15.800
But...

53:22.567 --> 53:25.933
[ID Card, Park Ae Sook]
There was a woman's ID inside.

53:26.733 --> 53:28.533
Do you think I'm some beggar?

53:28.533 --> 53:30.800
How could you give me some secondhand junk?

53:30.800 --> 53:32.600
Take it back!

53:34.233 --> 53:36.400
So I returned it.

53:36.400 --> 53:38.500
Who was that person?

53:39.200 --> 53:40.500
Some guy

53:40.500 --> 53:43.933
[Pig Café]
who works at the farm equipment repair shop.

53:44.967 --> 53:46.967
Im Seok Man.

53:46.967 --> 53:50.767
Seok Man saw me being taken away.

54:11.933 --> 54:14.900
Excuse me, are you Mr. Im Seok Man?

54:17.900 --> 54:21.000
I'm Reporter Seo Ji Won from Kangseng Daily.

54:21.000 --> 54:23.667
I have a few questions to ask you.

54:23.667 --> 54:26.733
Do you have a moment? It won't take long.

54:29.440 --> 54:31.424
Oh, dear.

54:35.467 --> 54:39.033
Oh, are you here for repair?

54:39.033 --> 54:42.433
Is there someone named Im Seok Man here?

54:42.433 --> 54:44.867
Try that store over there.

54:44.867 --> 54:46.067
Okay.

54:46.067 --> 54:51.067
Oh, Seok Man is quite popular.
A young lady came looking for him earlier.

54:51.067 --> 54:52.300
A young lady?

54:52.300 --> 54:55.400
Yeah, she was really pretty.

55:21.184 --> 55:26.202
[Seo Ji Won]

55:42.200 --> 55:44.320
Ouch!

55:44.320 --> 55:45.400
Ouch!

55:45.400 --> 55:46.667
Ji Won!

55:46.667 --> 55:48.667
Hey, Seo Ji Won!

55:48.667 --> 55:49.767
What are you doing, you little punk?

55:49.767 --> 55:51.967
Seo Ji Won, why are you here?
Are you hurt anywhere?

55:51.967 --> 55:54.333
No, it's nothing. It's nothing.

55:54.333 --> 55:58.200
I'm fine, I'm fine. Let go, quickly.

55:58.200 --> 56:01.633
Kang Tae Joo, why do you always
throw punches as soon as you see someone?

56:01.633 --> 56:02.967
- You...
- Hey!

56:02.967 --> 56:06.733
Seok Man was helping me remove the shards.

56:07.900 --> 56:10.833
Come on, there's one more here.

56:12.567 --> 56:14.267
Here, here.

56:14.267 --> 56:15.900
It's almost done.

56:22.367 --> 56:23.900
It's sharp. Please don't touch it.

56:23.900 --> 56:25.633
Oh, this...

56:27.500 --> 56:31.033
Ji Won, don't you recognize me?

56:31.033 --> 56:33.000
I'm Ki Beom's friend.

56:33.700 --> 56:35.167
You're Ki Beom's friend?

56:35.167 --> 56:38.600
You've paid for our drinks a few times.

56:38.600 --> 56:42.167
Oh? Oh yeah, right.

56:42.167 --> 56:44.333
Good to see you!

56:44.333 --> 56:45.933
Ji Won, blood...

56:50.967 --> 56:52.700
Thank you.

56:56.567 --> 57:01.167
So what brings you here, Reporter Seo?

57:01.167 --> 57:02.600
Well...

57:02.600 --> 57:05.500
Probably the same reason
as you, Detective Kang.

57:05.500 --> 57:07.267
- The purse!
- The witness?

57:08.133 --> 57:09.167
The purse?

57:09.167 --> 57:10.967
What witness?

57:16.000 --> 57:19.300
I found this purse.

57:19.300 --> 57:21.867
I didn't know there was an ID inside.

57:21.867 --> 57:23.333
I thought someone had thrown it away.

57:23.333 --> 57:26.533
Then you are the one
who left the purse in the bookstore?

57:27.500 --> 57:31.200
I thought if I left it there,
the owner would be able to find it.

57:31.200 --> 57:32.267
Why would you do that?

57:32.267 --> 57:35.667
You should have just put it back yourself.

57:37.200 --> 57:39.667
I was worried I'd be mistaken for a thief.

57:41.567 --> 57:42.600
This is driving me crazy.

57:42.600 --> 57:46.733
Wait, if this is all true, doesn't that mean
Ki Beom can clear his name?

57:46.733 --> 57:49.467
Right, if this guy just testifies.

57:49.467 --> 57:50.500
You'll testify, right?

57:50.500 --> 57:52.167
Of course I will. It's all because of me.

57:52.167 --> 57:53.433
Right, of course.

57:53.433 --> 57:54.533
Let's go, right away!

57:54.533 --> 57:56.567
Right... right now?

57:56.567 --> 57:58.333
Why? Is that a problem?

57:58.333 --> 58:00.733
Can I finish what I was working on first?

58:00.733 --> 58:02.500
The boss told me to finish it today.

58:02.500 --> 58:04.467
- How long will it take?
- 10 minutes, no...

58:04.467 --> 58:05.600
I can finish it in 5 minutes.

58:05.600 --> 58:07.233
Go ahead then.

58:07.233 --> 58:09.300
- I'll be right back.
- Alright.

58:14.133 --> 58:16.567
This is really good news.

58:16.567 --> 58:19.167
Ki Hwan and Sun Young
can finally breathe easier.

58:19.167 --> 58:21.000
You're right.

58:21.767 --> 58:23.500
Jeez, that kid.

58:23.500 --> 58:26.467
He witnessed Ki Beom

58:26.467 --> 58:28.133
being illegally detained...

58:39.100 --> 58:42.267
He was limping, like he was injured.

58:42.267 --> 58:44.000
I swear it's true!

58:50.767 --> 58:55.067
Hey, Tae Joo! Where are you going?

59:22.700 --> 59:24.633
High titanium levels would mean

59:24.633 --> 59:28.567
the person has been exposed
to a titanium-rich environment.

59:28.567 --> 59:34.100
He could be a worker in a factory
that handles alloys or welding.

59:34.100 --> 59:36.433
What about sodium and chlorine?

59:36.433 --> 59:40.300
Those are the main components of sweat.

59:40.300 --> 59:43.167
He's likely someone who sweats a lot.

59:43.167 --> 59:48.233
The killer could be a factory worker
who's constantly drenched in sweat,

59:48.233 --> 59:49.833
is that it?

59:49.833 --> 59:51.467
Probably.

59:56.167 --> 59:58.000
There you are.

01:00:01.367 --> 01:00:03.100
It's all done.

01:00:20.200 --> 01:00:22.733
As a police officer, it was my negligence.

01:00:24.300 --> 01:00:28.733
I should have realized sooner
that Ki Beom wasn't the real killer.

01:00:29.933 --> 01:00:31.933
Right.

01:00:31.933 --> 01:00:35.867
Only Ki Beom, who was innocent,
ended up suffering.

01:00:38.067 --> 01:00:39.733
Mr. Lee Yong Woo,

01:00:40.567 --> 01:00:43.633
don't you feel sorry for Ki Beom?

01:00:45.267 --> 01:00:47.033
Why would I?

01:00:48.600 --> 01:00:52.533
After all, Mr. Lee Yong Woo, he suffered

01:00:52.533 --> 01:00:54.733
because of your crimes, didn't he?

01:00:56.833 --> 01:00:59.233
It's not like I was the one
who put him in jail.

01:01:03.033 --> 01:01:04.800
You think so?

01:01:06.533 --> 01:01:11.767
Then is Ki Beom the friend you said you lost?

01:01:13.867 --> 01:01:16.533
I'll tell you that slowly.

01:01:19.067 --> 01:01:21.433
By the way, Professor,

01:01:22.433 --> 01:01:25.400
could you speak more casually?

01:01:25.400 --> 01:01:28.033
You were pretty casual with me back then.

01:01:29.933 --> 01:01:32.433
Is it because we haven't seen
each other in decades?

01:01:34.267 --> 01:01:36.600
You know me, right?

01:02:22.367 --> 01:02:23.367
Are you messing with me?

01:02:23.367 --> 01:02:24.867
What are you really up to?

01:02:24.867 --> 01:02:27.967
The special investigation team
has found another major suspect.

01:02:27.967 --> 01:02:29.700
The suspect is Im Seok Man, right?

01:02:29.700 --> 01:02:30.833
I need to check it out.

01:02:30.833 --> 01:02:32.467
Im Seok Man is type B.

01:02:32.467 --> 01:02:33.667
He's acquainted with Lee Ki Beom?

01:02:33.667 --> 01:02:37.167
If he's the real killer,
isn't that good for you too?

01:02:37.167 --> 01:02:39.800
I can't lose a friend like that again.

01:02:39.800 --> 01:02:42.800
So he was at the scene
of Lee Joo Hee's murder as well?

01:02:42.800 --> 01:02:45.733
Seok Man, what are you doing here
at this hour?

01:02:45.733 --> 01:02:48.133
I messed everything up.

01:02:48.133 --> 01:02:49.800
I...
